Gold Intelligence Engine
========================

This application consumes only free, publicly reachable data sources. No
credentials, API keys or paid subscriptions are required or embedded.

Attribution
-----------

U.S. Department of the Treasury — Daily Treasury Par Yield Curve Rates and
  Daily Treasury Par Real Yield Curve Rates. Public domain.
  https://home.treasury.gov

U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission — Commitments of Traders.
  Public domain.
  https://publicreporting.cftc.gov

Federal Reserve Bank of New York — Reference Rates (SOFR, EFFR). Public domain.
  https://markets.newyorkfed.org

Cboe Global Markets, Inc. — delayed index and equity quotes and daily history.
  Data is delayed and is used under attribution. (c) Cboe Global Markets, Inc.
  https://www.cboe.com

European Central Bank — euro foreign exchange reference rates, retrieved via
  the Frankfurter API. Attribution required.
  https://www.ecb.europa.eu / https://frankfurter.app

gold-api.com — spot gold and silver reference prices. Attribution required.
  https://api.gold-api.com

Yahoo Finance chart API — used only where a licence-restricted source is
  acceptable for DERIVED values. Raw values from this source are never
  published by the application.

Licence policy
--------------

A value whose licence class is not PUBLIC_DOMAIN or ATTRIBUTION is never
rendered raw in the user interface or returned raw by the REST API; only
derived quantities (z-scores, ranks, signs, factor scores) are exposed.
This rule is enforced in code, in the data contract, not only in documentation.

Disclaimer
----------

This software produces a statistical description of market conditions. It is
not investment advice, it does not publish a calibrated probability until a
live scoring record exists, and it reports the absence of a source rather than
substituting a guess.
